      "notes": "## Result summary\n- Outlook category: CanDoItAllSummaryTest\n- Message count: 1\n- Key sender: tomas.svo1@gmail.com\n- Subject: Tetris Game App\n\n## Evidence\n| Source (message id / link) | From | Received | Subject |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| AAMkAGRmMWViOTA2LTMzNGItNGNjNi1hMThmLWY2ZjA2ZTA1NjU4NwBGAAAAAABzw7m6jM_ATK0mFMmFWzQABwCKp9BRbAdVSoi7nuYgsTwNAAAAAAEMAACKp9BRbAdVSoi7nuYgsTwNAAUgXEn3AAA= | tomas.svo1@gmail.com | 2026-05-23T14:53:38Z | Tetris Game App |\n\nExcerpt (snippet): \"We need to program a simple Tetris game... The game should save the last maximum score achieved. However, we do not want a backend... We would need the application within one week at the latest.\"\n\n## Concrete findings\n- Request: Build simple Tetris as a website, keyboard controls (arrows or WASD).\n- Non-functional constraint: No backend; high score must be stored client-side (localStorage or equivalent).\n- Hosting: Static web hosting only; provide static build/artifacts.\n- Timeline: Delivery required within one week of 2026-05-23T14:53:38Z (deadline ~2026-05-30T14:53:38Z).\n- Mobile app: Interested but listed as a possible later phase.\n\n## Open gaps / questions\n- Confirmation needed: Is a single-player local-only leaderboard sufficient (localStorage) or is any syncing expected later?\n- Acceptance criteria: required screen sizes, accessibility, supported browsers, and target devices.\n- UX details: scoring rules, levels, sound, and graphics expectations.\n- Build/hosting constraints: specific static host (Netlify, GitHub Pages) or custom domain/setup?\n- Payment/contract/approval not provided in message.\n\n## Recommended next actions\n1. Confirm scope and deadline with requester immediately (ask about acceptance criteria, browsers, and hosting preferences).\n2. Produce a short implementation plan and estimate for web-only MVP (keyboard controls + local high score) within 48 hours.\n3. Assign development tasks for web MVP with deadline aligned to requested delivery date.\n4. Prepare static build and deployment instructions; validate on a common static host.\n5. Send delivery package and request formal acceptance from requester once deployed.",
